From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:59:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: don't re-arm req_event while polling in process_ring

tapdisk_xenio_ctx_process_ring() unconditionally set final=1,
requesting a further notification (req_event re-arm) at the end of
each processed batch. While the ring is being polled, the event
channel is masked and the stop-polling callback already performs
this final check before going back to sleep.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/td-ctx.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/td-ctx.c b/drivers/td-ctx.c
index ced0563f..c2c108e3 100644
--- a/drivers/td-ctx.c
+++ b/drivers/td-ctx.c
@@ -284,7 +284,16 @@ tapdisk_xenio_ctx_process_ring(struct td_blkif_queue *queue, bool final)
         queue->n_reqs_free -= n_reqs;
         ASSERT(queue->n_reqs_free <= queue->ring_size);
         limit -= n_reqs;
-        final = 1;
+
+        /*
+         * While polling, the ring's event channel is masked and the
+         * stop-polling callback performs the final check (re-arming
+         * req_event) before we go back to sleep. Re-arming here would only
+         * make the frontend issue a notification hypercall per request that
+         * nobody waits for.
+         */
+        if (!queue->in_polling)
+            final = 1;
 
         if (unlikely(reqs[(n_reqs - 1)]->operation ==
                      BLKIF_OP_WRITE_BARRIER)) {
